] [17592186424571 1079 #uuid "ab5409cf-4685-540d-8e56-731571e9e2ff" 13194139534534 17592186045417 true] [17592186424572 1075 #edb/ref 17592186424539 13194139534534 17592186045417 true] [17592186424572 1075 #edb/ref 17592186424549 13194139534534 17592186045417 true] [17592186424572 1075 #edb/ref 17592186424556 13194139534534 17592186045417 true] [17592186424572 1075 #edb/ref 17592186424561 13194139534534 17592186045417 true] [17592186424572 1075 #edb/ref 17592186424563 13194139534534 17592186045417 true] [17592186424572 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534534 17592186045417 true] [17592186424572 1077 "selection" 13194139534534 17592186045417 true] [17592186424572 1078 #edb/ref 17592186424561 13194139534534 17592186045417 true] [17592186424572 1079 #uuid "ebf5a599-01b3-5f07-9129-5e078a5628ad" 13194139534534 17592186045417 true] [17592186424573 1068 #edb/ref 17592186424568 13194139534534 17592186045417 true] [17592186424573 1069 "q-132193" 13194139534534 17592186045417 true] [17592186424573 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534534 17592186045417 true] [17592186424573 1071 "Given that the random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(\\sqrt{2}),$ calculate $P(X>\\sqrt{2}).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places." 13194139534534 17592186045417 true] [17592186424573 1072 #uuid "04d4be2b-e767-5839-99c5-470d8cac4dc9" 13194139534534 17592186045417 true] [17592186424573 1074 "An exponential random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda $ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\lambda {e}^{-\\lambda x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\nX∼\\text{Exp}(\\sqrt{2}).\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2}{e}^{-\\sqrt{2}x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $P(X>\\sqrt{2})$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>\\sqrt{2}) & ={\\int }_{\\sqrt{2}}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\sqrt{2}}^{\\infty }\\sqrt{2}{e}^{-\\sqrt{2}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{-\\sqrt{2}x}{|}_{\\sqrt{2}}^{\\infty } \\\\  & ={e}^{-2} \\\\  & ≈0.1353\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534534 17592186045417 true] [17592186424574 1068 #edb/ref 17592186424566 13194139534534 17592186045417 true] [17592186424574 1069 "q-253935" 13194139534534 17592186045417 true] [17592186424574 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534534 17592186045417 true] [17592186424574 1071 "Given that the random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(3),$ calculate $P(X\\le \\frac{5}{6}\\,|\\,X>\\frac{2}{3}).$" 13194139534534 17592186045417 true] [17592186424574 1072 #uuid "15d3a8f7-57e9-5955-b347-e7b15292f88f" 13194139534534 17592186045417 true] [17592186424574 1074 "Given a random variable $X∼Exp(\\lambda ),$ and two positive real numbers $s,t,$ the memoryless property of the exponential distribution states that\n\n$$\nP(X>s+t\\,|\\,X>s)=P(X>t)={e}^{-\\lambda t}.\n$$\n\nWe can compute the complementary conditional probability as follows:\n\n$$\nP(X\\le s+t\\,|\\,X>s)=1-P(X>s+t\\,|\\,X>s)=1-{e}^{-\\lambda t}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $\\lambda =3,$ $s=\\frac{2}{3},$ and $s+t=\\frac{5}{6}.$ From this, we can find $t$ as follows:\n\n$$\nt=(t+s)-s=\\frac{5}{6}-\\frac{2}{3}=\\frac{1}{6}\n$$\n\nSubstituting these values into the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le \\frac{5}{6}\\,|\\,X>\\frac{2}{3}) & =1-{e}^{-\\lambda t} \\\\  & =1-{e}^{-(3)\\cdot (1/6)} \\\\  & =1-{e}^{-1/2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534534 17592186045417 true] [17592186424575 1068 #edb/ref 17592186424567 13194139534534 17592186045417 true] [17592186424575 1069 "q-132173" 13194139534534 17592186045417 true] [17592186424575 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534534 17592186045417 true] [17592186424575 1071 "Given that the random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(\\frac{1}{5}),$ calculate $P(X\\le 2).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places." 13194139534534 17592186045417 true] [17592186424575 1072 #uuid "377d9ecb-b1f2-5b7d-b293-34044d6f6558" 13194139534534 17592186045417 true] [17592186424575 1074 "An exponential random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda $ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\lambda {e}^{-\\lambda x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\nX∼\\text{Exp}(\\frac{1}{5}).\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{5}{e}^{-x/5}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $P(X\\le 2)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 2) & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{5}{e}^{-x/5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{{e}^{-x/5}|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-2/5}+{e}^{0} \\\\  & ≈0.3297\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534534 17592186045417 true] [17592186424576 1068 #edb/ref 17592186424565 13194139534534 17592186045417 true] [17592186424576 1069 "q-132179" 13194139534534 17592186045417 true] [17592186424576 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534534 17592186045417 true] [17592186424576 1071 "Given that the random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(\\sqrt{3}),$ calculate $P(X<\\frac{1}{3}).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places." 13194139534534 17592186045417 true] [17592186424576 1072 #uuid "4b3ef3ac-d2db-5eb8-8c5f-a033b26be69b" 13194139534534 17592186045417 true] [17592186424576 1074 "An exponential random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda $ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\lambda {e}^{-\\lambda x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\nX∼\\text{Exp}(\\sqrt{3}).\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}{e}^{-\\sqrt{3}x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $P(X<\\frac{1}{3})$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<\\frac{1}{3}) & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/3}\\sqrt{3}{e}^{-\\sqrt{3}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{-\\sqrt{3}x}{|}_{0}^{1/3} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-\\sqrt{3}/3}+{e}^{0} \\\\  & ≈0.4386\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534534 17592186045417 true] [17592186424577 1068 #edb/ref 17592186424572 13194139534534 17592186045417 true] [17592186424577 1069 "q-96347" 13194139534534 17592186045417 true] [17592186424577 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534534 17592186045417 true] [17592186424577 1071 "Given that the random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(\\frac{1}{3}),$ calculate $P(2<X<3).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places." 13194139534534 17592186045417 true] [17592186424577 1072 #uuid "9bd8d602-6713-5d8a-8e29-384c77e10125" 13194139534534 17592186045417 true] [17592186424577 1074 "An exponential random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda $ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\lambda {e}^{-\\lambda x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\nX∼\\text{Exp}(\\frac{1}{3}).\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-x/3}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $P(2<X<3)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(2<X<3) & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-x/3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{-x/3}{|}_{2}^{3} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-1}+{e}^{-2/3} \\\\  & ≈0.1455\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534534 17592186045417 true] [17592186424578 1068 #edb/ref 17592186424569 13194139534534 17592186045417 true] [17592186424578 1069 "q-253936" 13194139534534 17592186045417 true] [17592186424578 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534534 17592186045417 true] [17592186424578 1071 "Given that the random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(\\frac{3}{5}),$ calculate $P(X\\le 9\\,|\\,X>4).$" 13194139534534 17592186045417 true] [17592186424578 1072 #uuid "a86905dc-6d69-50e5-afb3-4d8bb353dbfd" 13194139534534 17592186045417 true] [17592186424578 1074 "Given a random variable $X∼Exp(\\lambda ),$ and two positive real numbers $s,t,$ the memoryless property of the exponential distribution states that\n\n$$\nP(X>s+t\\,|\\,X>s)=P(X>t)={e}^{-\\lambda t}.\n$$\n\nWe can compute the complementary conditional probability as follows:\n\n$$\nP(X\\le s+t\\,|\\,X>s)=1-P(X>s+t\\,|\\,X>s)=1-{e}^{-\\lambda t}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $\\lambda =\\frac{3}{5},$ $s=4,$ and $s+t=9.$ From this, we can find $t$ as follows:\n\n$$\nt=(t+s)-s=9-4=5\n$$\n\nSubstituting these values into the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 9\\,|\\,X>4) & =1-{e}^{-\\lambda t} \\\\  & =1-{e}^{-(3/5)\\cdot (5)} \\\\  & =1-{e}^{-3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534534 17592186045417 true] [17592186424579 1068 #edb/ref 17592186424570 13194139534534 17592186045417 true] [17592186424579 1069 "q-96412" 13194139534534 17592186045417 true] [17592186424579 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534534 17592186045417 true] [17592186424579 1071 "Given that the random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(8),$ calculate $P(X>0.4).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places." 13194139534534 17592186045417 true] [17592186424579 1072 #uuid "be9c7f67-1bb2-5f32-8555-0a5418fba86d" 13194139534534 17592186045417 true] [17592186424579 1074 "An exponential random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda $ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\lambda {e}^{-\\lambda x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\nX∼\\text{Exp}(8).\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}8{e}^{-8x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $P(X>0.4)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>0.4) & ={\\int }_{0.4}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0.4}^{\\infty }8{e}^{-8x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{-8x}{|}_{0.4}^{\\infty } \\\\  & ={e}^{-3.2} \\\\  & ≈0.0408\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534534 17592186045417 true] [17592186424580 1068 #edb/ref 17592186424571 13194139534534 17592186045417 true] [17592186424580 1069 "q-96421" 13194139534534 17592186045417 true] [17592186424580 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534534 17592186045417 true] [17592186424580 1071 "Given that the random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(1),$ calculate $P(0.5\\le X\\le 2).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places." 13194139534534 17592186045417 true] [17592186424580 1072 #uuid "d71bf438-c740-5ac5-956a-edf3ba9d43d6" 13194139534534 17592186045417 true] [17592186424580 1074 "An exponential random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda $ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\lambda {e}^{-\\lambda x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\nX∼\\text{Exp}(1).\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $P(0.5\\le X\\le 2)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0.5\\le X\\le 2) & ={\\int }_{0.5}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0.5}^{2}{e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{-x}{|}_{0.5}^{2} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-2}+{e}^{-0.5} \\\\  & ≈0.4712\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534534 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-016959b9-f05f-53b3-afd3-07e994e53882" 17592186424525 "answer-0720396c-abfc-53ff-8ef1-c514b74b2d21" 17592186424526 "answer-13134444-762f-50b4-bf4c-6865257862e6" 17592186424527 "answer-15122c8a-6495-57b5-bc9a-8504dc7b9d5f" 17592186424528 "answer-17f972c0-e3f4-509a-b28c-755fd028d943" 17592186424529 "answer-25462498-9604-5abf-a03e-8496f16cbe50" 17592186424530 "answer-25fb97a5-9ed6-5c98-8031-485552414117" 17592186424531 "answer-2840ed6b-1f83-568f-87c3-170c58ac5221" 17592186424532 "answer-2fc40c2d-1af0-5adc-a2bc-6557e8adc194" 17592186424533 "answer-31011ded-b236-51be-8752-9a8a39f1aa2a" 17592186424534 "answer-3a08e9d4-be37-5bcd-b93a-f75705061f0d" 17592